<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan buys 54,000 tonnes U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 54,000 tonnes U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's CK group on Tuesday bought a shipment of 54,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 corn from Tradi Grain of the United States, traders said.  </p>
<p>The CK Group comprises Chia Hsin Flour Feed and Vegetable Oil Corp and some buyers from Taiwan's southern port city of Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>Details for the Tuesday tender are as follows:</p>
<p>Tonnes  Date/Location</p>
<p>	   U.S. Gulf    Pacific Northwest Price/Futures</p>
<p> 54,000  August 1-15  August 16-30	81.88 UScents/September</p>
<p> 54,000  August 1-15  August 16-30	US$124.99</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
</text>
